23:["$","$L28",null,{"items":[{"question":"How many Paras (Juz) and pages are in the Holy Quran?","answer":"The Holy Quran contains 30 Paras (Juz) and 114 Surahs. The standard King Fahd Complex Madani Mushaf has exactly 604 pages, structured at 20 pages per Juz (with Juz 30 spanning 23 pages). Indo-Pak 16-line editions generally span 548 pages, and 13-line prints span 848 pages."},{"question":"How many Sajdah Tilawat are in the Quran and which is the first Sajdah?","answer":"There are 14 agreed-upon Sajdah Tilawat in the Holy Quran according to the Hanafi, Shafi’i, and Hanbali schools. The first sajdah in Quran occurs in Surah Al-A’raf (7:206) in Para 9."},{"question":"What is the shortest surah in the Quran?","answer":"The shortest surah in the Quran is Surah Al-Kawthar (Chapter 108), which has only 3 verses, 10 words, and 42 letters."},{"question":"What is Dua Khatam Quran and its significance?","answer":"Dua Khatam Quran is the supplication made upon completing the entire Quran recitation. Supplications made at the conclusion of Khatam are accepted with immense divine blessing and mercy."},{"question":"Where can I download the Quran book and study materials?","answer":"You can download the Quran 30 Para Guide PDF directly from our website at /quran, with verified links to King Fahd Complex 15-line Madani Mushafs and 16-line Indo-Pak editions."}],"title":"Key Questions & Rulings Answered"}]
